/-!
# The Cantor basis

`CANTOR_BASIS_128` lists `v_0 = 1, v_1, …, v_127` with `v_i^2 + v_i = v_(i-1)` in the tower.
The first `2^k` vectors lie in level `k` (`cantorV_lt`) and form a basis of it over `GF(2)`:
every element is a sum of some of them (`cantor_span`), in only one way (`cantor_injective`).
The relations are checked by the kernel on the stored integers, in chunks that keep each check
small, and the basis property by exhibiting the inverse change of basis.
-/

open Aeneas Aeneas.Std CoreModels Polynomial
open ConcreteBinaryTower ConcreteBinaryTower.Coordinates
open p3_binary_field BinaryField
open Plonky3Lean.Lib Plonky3Lean.Spec.BinaryField

